{
  "dom_id": "step-q183527",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Find the missing entries in the following table:\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| Whenever $A,$ then $B$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $A$ whenever $B$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $A,$ provided that $B$ | {{field-3}} |",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the implication $P⇒Q:$\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nLet's now compare these against the entries in our table:\n\n- \"Whenever $A,$ then $B$\" means $A⇒B$\n\n- \"$A$ whenever $B$\" means $B⇒A$\n\n- \"$A,$ provided that $B$\" means $B⇒A$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| Whenever $A,$ then $B$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $A$ whenever $B$ | $B⇒A$ |\n| $A,$ provided that $B$ | $B⇒A$ |",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
